  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I checked the courier records for all four orders. Two were late enough to compensate and two weren't, so I've added **$30.00** in account credit.\n\n**K-6501, Saffron Lane (tonight): $25.00 credit**\nIt was due at 6:00 PM and reached you at 6:52 PM, so 52 minutes late. For 45+ minutes late, you get 20% of the food subtotal ($128.00), which comes to $25.60. Plus members can get up to $25 for this, so I've added $25.00.\n\n**K-6502, Pho Real (Thursday): $5.00 credit**\nIt was due at 7:15 PM and reached you at 7:45 PM, so 30 minutes late. For 16\u201344 minutes late, Plus orders get a $5.00 credit.\n\n**K-6503, Taqueria Luz (Tuesday): no credit**\nThe original time was 6:30 PM, but at 5:50 PM you got a push notification moving it to 7:00 PM. When we send an updated time at least 30 minutes ahead, the new time counts as the promised time. The order arrived at 7:12 PM, 12 minutes after that. An order only counts as late if it arrives more than 15 minutes after the promised time, so this one doesn't qualify.\n\n**K-6504, Burger Barn (last Friday, Oct 16): no credit**\nThis one was late: due at 7:00 PM, delivered at 8:00 PM. But we can only compensate a late order up to 7 days after it's delivered, and that window closed on the evening of Oct 23.\n\nYour $30.00 credit is on your account now and will apply to your next orders. I'm sorry this week's deliveries were so frustrating. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thanks for checking all four. I'm not going to argue about the details, but I'd like to understand the two that got nothing. For Taqueria Luz, the notification moved it to 7:00 and it still came at 7:12, which feels late to me. And Burger Barn was over an hour late, so I don't see why the date window matters if I only found out about it now.\n\nAlso, there's something else I need to raise. The Pho Real order on Thursday, #6502, was missing the summer rolls. I paid for them and they weren't in the bag. I'd like those compensated, and I'd prefer account credit for them."
  },
