  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand why those two feel unfair. Here's what's behind each one.\n\n**Taqueria Luz (K-6503):** The updated time was sent at 5:50 PM, 40 minutes before the original 6:30 PM time. Because you were told in advance, 7:00 PM became the promised time. A delivery counts as late only if it arrives more than 15 minutes after that. At 12 minutes, this one was under the threshold. I know it still felt late.\n\n**Burger Barn (K-6504):** It was over an hour late, and you'd normally have been owed credit. But the 7-day limit runs from when the order is delivered, not from when it's reported. It's a fixed limit with no exceptions, so I can't compensate this order. I'm sorry.\n\n**Missing summer rolls (K-6502):** You reported this in time (we accept missing items up to 48 hours after delivery), and nothing had been refunded for them yet. As credit, you'd get the price plus 20%, which is $10.80. But you can receive at most $40 in credit per conversation, and with the $30 from earlier, that would bring it to $40.80. When credit would go over that limit, I have to refund to your card instead. So I've refunded **$9.00** (the price of the summer rolls) to your Visa ending 4242. It should appear in 3\u20135 business days.\n\nToday's total:\n- **$30.00 account credit** (late deliveries on K-6501 and K-6502)\n- **$9.00 card refund** (missing summer rolls on K-6502)\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I'll accept that. The Taqueria Luz explanation makes sense even though it still feels late to me.\n\nFor the summer rolls, I'm fine with the card refund instead of credit. Just to confirm, the $9.00 goes to my Visa ending 4242 and should show up in 3 to 5 business days?\n\nAlso, I'd like you to double-check the Burger Barn decision. It was an hour late and I only found out this week that I could report it, so I'm not happy about that one. But I understand you're telling me it's final.\n\nThanks for sorting out the others.\n\n\n<br>"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Yes, that's right. The $9.00 refund (reference RF-4000) is going to your Visa ending 4242 and should show up in 3\u20135 business days.\n\nI double-checked Burger Barn (K-6504). The courier record shows it was delivered at 8:00 PM on October 16. That's an hour late, so you're right that it was late enough for credit. But the 7-day reporting window closed at 8:00 PM on October 23, about a day before you contacted us. The window runs from delivery, not from when you find out you can report it. I'm sorry; I know that's frustrating when the order really was that late.\n\nIf you'd still like a person to look at it, tell me and I'll pass it to a specialist, who will follow up within 24 hours. I can't promise they'll decide differently.\n\nHere's what we did today:\n- **$30.00 account credit**, already on your account for your next orders\n- **$9.00 refund** to your Visa ending 4242\n\nThanks for your patience with all of this, Monique. I hope your next orders arrive on time."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Thanks for double-checking Burger Barn. I'd like a specialist to look at it, so please pass it on. I understand they may not decide differently.\n\nThanks for the $9.00 refund reference, RF-4000. I'll keep an eye on the Visa for it. And I appreciate the $30 credit for the other two.\n\nThat's everything from me."
